3. Implanted cardiac pacemaker or other electronic devices;
4. Prior treatment with transcutaneous auricular vagus nerve stimulation (taVNS);
5. Known malignancy;
6. Severe cardiovascular/cerebrovascular, hepatic, or renal diseases;
7. Cognitive impairment, psychiatric disorders, or other conditions that may affect patient cooperation;
8. Refusal to sign informed consent.

