Contraindications to remote ischemic conditioning (RIC), including:

1. Peripheral vascular disease of the upper or lower extremities, particularly significant stenosis or occlusion of the brachial, ulnar, or radial arteries, or any condition considered by the investigator to make upper-arm cuff inflation for RIC unsuitable;
